# [IDR](../wg/idr.html)

## Summary

The IDR Working Group met at IETF 126 (Session 1) to discuss core BGP protocol updates, Segment Routing (SR), SR Traffic Engineering (SRTE), BGP Link-State (BGP-LS), and multicast policy routing. Key discussions centered on signaling tunnel encapsulation for MASQUE, the controversial BGP Unreachable Prefix Announcement (UPA) v2 proposal, hierarchical route reflection improvements for Route Target Constrain (RTC), and various SR/BGP-LS extensions.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### 1. Welcome and WG Status
* **Presenter**: Susan Hares
* **Slides**: [1-0. IDR Chairs Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-idr-sessa-1-0-idr-chairs-slides-00)
* **Details**: The IDR charter has been approved. The chairs have split drafts into parallel queues: BGP Core, SR/SRTE, BGP-LS, and Flowspec to streamline progress. 

